WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.309 --> 00:00:11.959
Last year, Vicki Hollub pulled off one of
the biggest coups in the history of big oil.

00:00:11.959 --> 00:00:18.200
But just months later, the CEO of Houston-based
Occidental Petroleum was scrambling to save

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.310
her job and her company.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:27.580
The $55bn acquisition of Anadarko Petroleum
was a remarkable victory for Hollub.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:32.439
Not only did she gatecrash a planned deal
by larger rival Chevron, but the Oxy boss

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:37.070
brought Warren Buffett’s Berkshire Hathaway
to the party as an investor to help pay for

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.070
the megadeal.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:44.129
Not invited were Oxy shareholders, including
the feared activist raider Carl Icahn, who

00:00:44.129 --> 00:00:47.580
didn't get to vote on the deal thanks to how
the deal was structured.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.839
But victory did not come cheap.

00:00:49.839 --> 00:00:56.839
Oxy’s debt soared to $43.9bn, or six times
higher than the level it was at just a year

00:00:56.839 --> 00:00:57.839
prior.

00:00:57.839 --> 00:01:03.739
Then came the twin pressures of Covid-19 and
a price war between Russia and Saudi Arabia.

00:01:03.739 --> 00:01:08.409
The oil price crash emboldened Carl Icahn,
who built his stake to over 10 per cent of

00:01:08.409 --> 00:01:09.580
the company’s shares.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:15.619
In a desperate move, Hollub introduced a poison
pill to stop Icahn from taking over the company.

00:01:15.619 --> 00:01:20.850
A poison pill allows a firm to issue new shares
which dilute an unwanted suitor’s stake

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.320
in the company.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:28.249
Hollub also broke her biggest promise to investors:
she slashed the dividend almost 90 per cent,

00:01:28.249 --> 00:01:30.799
the first payout cut in three decades.

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:35.409
To preserve cash, Oxy recut its deal with
Buffett, giving him shares in the company

00:01:35.409 --> 00:01:37.909
in lieu of promised cash payments.

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:44.520
Finally, Icahn made his move, gaining four
seats on Oxy’s 11-person board.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:49.590
As markets and the oil price recovered, Oxy’s
share price has recouped some of its losses.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:53.770
But it sits far below where it was before
the Anadarko deal.

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:57.679
And that is why Hollub’s big deal backfired.

